  "published": "2026-09-23T10:17:11Z",
  "modified": "2026-09-23T10:17:11Z",
  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: assertion failures in named when handling DNS messages\n     whose CLASS is not IN or that use the meta-classes ANY or NONE\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-5946-1.patch: force recursion off and set the\n       allow-recursion ACLs to none for views with a class other than IN\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-5946-2.patch: return NOTIMP for UPDATE and\n       NOTIFY in non-IN views, check the class before treating WKS rdata as\n       class IN, and assert that updated zones are class IN\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-5946-3.patch: validate the message CLASS early,\n       returning NOTIMP for unsupported classes and FORMERR for NONE outside\n       UPDATE and ANY outside TKEY negotiation\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-5946-4.patch: reject UPDATE and NOTIFY messages\n       whose question class is ANY or NONE with FORMERR\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-5946-5.patch: skip deny-answer-address matching\n       for non-IN address records\n     - CVE-2026-5946",
